-- chem/onecentre.cub — the one integral atoms' determinants rest on, for s-type radial functions P(r)·e^{−αr} about one
-- centre (P a polynomial with rational coefficients, α a positive rational), exactly, in rationals. The one function is
-- the tail polynomial: ∫_r^∞ P(t) e^{−qt} dt = R(r) e^{−qr} with qR − R′ = P, so R = (P + R′)/q = Σ_k P^{(k)}/q^{k+1}
-- (`oc-tail`), and ∫_0^∞ P e^{−qt} dt = R(0) = Σ_k k!·p_k/q^{k+1} (`oc-int`). Everything else is an instance, with the
-- angular factor 4π of each electron dropped throughout (it cancels in every quotient below):
--   overlap ⟨f, g⟩ = ∫ f g r² dr;  ⟨f, r⁻¹ g⟩ = ∫ f g r dr;  kinetic ⟨f, −½Δ g⟩ = −½ ∫ f (r² g″ + 2r g′) dr,
--   g′ = (Q′ − βQ) e^{−βr} for g = Q e^{−βr};
--   repulsion of two s-densities d = D e^{−pr}, e = E e^{−qr}:  ∫∫ d(r₁) e(r₂) r_>⁻¹ r₁² r₂² dr₁ dr₂
--     = ∫ d r₁ [∫_0^{r₁} e t² dt] dr₁ + ∫ d r₁² [∫_{r₁}^∞ e t dt] dr₁
--     = (∫ d r)(∫ e t²) − ∫ D·R_a r e^{−(p+q)r} + ∫ D·R_b r² e^{−(p+q)r},   R_a = tail of t²E, R_b = tail of tE.
-- Checked, at the charges Z = 1, 2, 3, 3/2 (each integral is a monomial in Z by r → r/Z, so one charge fixes each
-- identity): hydrogen's 1s and 2s levels −Z²/2 and −Z²/8, their orthogonality, ⟨1s1s|r₁₂⁻¹|1s1s⟩ = 5Z/8, the direct
-- and exchange integrals of 1s with 2s, 17Z/81 and 16Z/729, the 1s² determinant of the two-electron ion −Z² + 5Z/8,
-- and the 1s²2s determinant of lithium with hydrogenic orbitals of charge 3 (`oc-li`).
-- Taken here, not proved: that the angular average of 1/r₁₂ over two s-densities is 1/r_> (Newton's shell theorem);
-- the Slater rules for the energy of a determinant of orthonormal orbitals, E = Σ h + Σ_pairs (J − K·[same spin]);
-- −½Δ on a radial function as −½(g″ + 2g′/r); and the integral ∫_0^∞ t^k e^{−qt} dt = k!/q^{k+1} behind the tail.
import "laplace.hypercubical"

